# Third-party notices

Eidnara is licensed under the MIT License (see `LICENSE`).

This file indexes third-party notices that ship inside the repository. Each
migration wave that carries a third-party component adds a row here and keeps
the component's own `NOTICE` file next to the code it covers.

| Component | Location | Arrives in wave |
|---|---|---|
| Secret-scanner rules (gossip-rs derived) | `crates/secret-scanner/NOTICE` | U4 |
| ONNX Runtime and bundled model | `packages/host-linux-x64-gnu/NOTICE` | U7 |

No third-party component is present yet. The table is the contract for where
each notice must land. The owning wave's receipt lists the notice file as a
`verbatim` copy from the source repository.
